invariant: INV-26
file: gcm.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm.c guards its call to the multi-block counter mode on a macro no
  build defines, so a host object runs every block of counter mode
  through the one-block cipher on a schedule the instructions run, and
  pays the per-block call and wipe that docs/performance.md measured.
  Nothing else objects: gcm_counter_blocks_hw still links, and every
  vector and equivalence test passes, because both paths compute the same
  bytes. The script compiles gcm.c for each host object at -O2 and
  requires its object to call gcm_counter_blocks_hw; at -O0, gcc would
  still emit the static function that holds the call.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    off = counter_mode_whole_blocks(k, counter, in, n, out);
#endif
--- new
#ifdef CH_COUNTER_BLOCKS_HW
    off = counter_mode_whole_blocks(k, counter, in, n, out);
#endif
